      "description": "<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The diatha takes acid, electricity, fire, piercing, slashing, or sonic damage</p>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The diatha has 5 or fewer Hit Points</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The diatha dies, its body combusting in a flash of flame. All creatures in a 5-foot-radius emanation take 1d6 Fire Damage damage (Basic DC 16 Reflex Saving Throw save).</p>",
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "name": "Hydrocarbon Slick",
      "actions": null,
      "traits": [
        "fire"
      ],
      "description": "<p>If a diatha dies before it can detonate, its body rapidly decomposes into a slick of highly volatile hydrocarbons. Any effect that deals acid, electricity, or fire damage in an area that includes the square where the diatha died, or targets a creature in that square, causes a small explosion and consumes the slick.</p>\n<p>All creatures in the square and in a 5ft Type:emanation take 1d6 Fire Damage damage (Basic DC 16 Reflex Saving Throw save). The slick evaporates after 10 minutes if it isn't ignited.</p>",
      "collapsed": false
    }
